Package: terminal-router
Version: 1.3.6
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: bash, tmux (>= 3.0), python3, tio
Recommends: cron
Suggests: terminator
Maintainer: Franco Conidi aka edmond <fconidi@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://www.syslinuxos.com
Description: Terminal Router - tmux session recorder for AI-assisted router work
 Records every interactive terminal session into a per-pane log file under
 ~/.claude-logs, so an AI assistant such as Claude Code can follow a live
 network device CLI session in real time by reading a single file.
 .
 The typical use case is an interactive SSH session on a Cisco or Huawei
 router: the assistant has no access to the device and never needs any. The
 operator types, the assistant reads the log and suggests, the operator
 decides what to run.
 .
 Features:
  - Integrated workspace: router and live Claude/Codex observer panes side by side
  - tio serial-console dependency and connection hint for USB adapters
  - AI follows only the router pane, accepts questions and never sends commands
  - Dedicated tmux server keeps the assistant pane out of captured logs
  - Every interactive terminal enters its own tmux session automatically
  - "terminal-router launch" logs a single self-contained session instead,
    with no ~/.bashrc, ~/.zshrc or ~/.tmux.conf edits at all
  - status, install and launch warn if neither claude nor codex is on PATH,
    since the log has no AI assistant to read it otherwise
  - Each pane (session, window, split) is logged to its own timestamped file
  - Stable ~/.claude-logs/latest symlink always points at the newest pane
  - logpause / logresume kill-switch for sensitive work
  - pause / resume commands also available in one-shot launch sessions
  - doctor checks setup, permissions and live tmux panes without changing them
  - Strict permissions: directory 0700, log files 0600
  - Automatic rotation: logs older than 30 days deleted nightly at 03:00
  - Clean removal: terminal-router remove undoes every change, with backups
 .
 All configuration is per-user and confined to $HOME. Nothing is enabled at
 install time: the user must explicitly opt in from the menu entry or with
 "terminal-router install", after acknowledging that the log captures whatever
 is printed on screen.
Installed-Size: 208
